  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/25452a43-0a8d-4a53-afa0-69d4c22a91b0-image.png\" style=\"width: 301px; height: 242px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>The Diagram shown in the question represents the balanced wheatstone bridge. It satisfy the condition of balanced wheat stone bridge.<br />Multiplication of dimensionally opposite resistance is same.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br />When the circuit is balanced wheat stone bridge then current through the branch&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;is zero, so it can be removed.</p><p>Now, after removing&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;wire voltage across&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p>So, current will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;</p>",
